  "details": "While reading another tracked suggest about warp effects on exit ( https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/add-warp-effects-when-closing-vrchat ) it crossed my mind that there really should, as a matter of polish, be an optional 'default' warp-in and warp-out effect for everyone who hasn't yet purchased a custom one. Something fairly neutral and silent, but pleasent enough provide a slightly more 'polished' look to all player arrivals and departures.\n\nThis also then made me think, that if it is the job of the player's client to send the signal to other clients to play a specific warp effect (including maybe a 'blank' effect if a player doesn't want any warp effect at all), that this could also then mean it could help act as a crash indicator.\n\nThat being, if other clients get the 'player has left session' signal but don't get told which warp-out to play before the player disconnected, that it could then be deduced that the other client disconnected due to a crash or network issue. This could then in turn make a specific 'unexpected disconnect' warp-out effect play instead that would let others know the player didn't leave the instance willingly!",
